# =============================================================================
# Docker build-context ignore list - REPOSITORY ROOT (AAP 0.1.1.3, 0.2.1.3).
#
# THE BUILD CONTEXT IS THE REPOSITORY ROOT, so this single file governs BOTH
# image builds:
#   docker/docker-compose.yml -> both services declare `build.context: ..`
#   docker build -f docker/api.Dockerfile      -t dnnmigration-api      .
#   docker build -f docker/frontend.Dockerfile -t dnnmigration-frontend .
# (frontend/.dockerignore is a separate file that applies only to a
#  frontend-rooted context; it does NOT apply to the builds above.)
#
# NEVER EXCLUDE - every item below is COPYd by a Dockerfile, and its absence
# breaks an image build in a way no compiler catches:
#   backend/           global.json, Directory.Build.props, DnnMigration.sln,
#                      all six *.csproj, src/**/*.cs, all appsettings*.json
#   frontend/          package.json AND package-lock.json (`npm ci` fails
#                      outright without the lockfile - AAP 0.6.2), angular.json,
#                      tsconfig*.json, karma.conf.js, .nvmrc, src/**, public/**
#   docker/nginx.conf  COPYd by docker/frontend.Dockerfile; the frontend image
#                      build fails at that COPY step if it is missing
#                      (AAP 0.5.1.9, 0.9.3)
#
# Consequently there is NO blanket rule for backend/, frontend/ or docker/, and
# NO `!` re-inclusion anywhere in this file: every rule is either root-anchored
# or `**/`-scoped, so rule ordering can never resurrect or hide a required file.
#
# Effect: the context shrinks from ~47 MB to well under 1 MB, because the legacy
# reference trees below account for ~35 MB of it and no image copies a byte.
# =============================================================================

# Version control and repository plumbing.
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github/

# Legacy VB.NET reference trees - never copied into an image.
# Library/ (8.8 MB, 576 files) and Website/ (26 MB, 1754 files) are read-only
# .NET Framework 2.0 reference inputs (AAP 0.2.1.4) and stay byte-identical on
# disk (AAP 0.9.5); excluding them here is a build-context optimisation only.
Library/
Website/
DotNetNuke.sln
DotNetNuke_VS2008.sln

# Documentation and repository metadata - no image serves documentation.
docs/
blitzy/
mkdocs.yml
catalog-info.yaml
README.md
MIGRATION_NOTES.md
# Any other root-level Markdown. Root-scoped on purpose: `*` never crosses `/`,
# so nested files such as frontend/README.md are deliberately left untouched.
*.md

# .NET build output.
# Load-bearing, not cosmetic: docker/api.Dockerfile runs `dotnet restore` inside
# the SDK stage and only afterwards does `COPY backend/ ./` followed by
# `dotnet publish --no-restore`. A host-built obj/ reaching the context would
# overwrite the container's project.assets.json with host paths and break that
# publish. These rules are intentionally GLOBAL, unlike .gitignore which scopes
# them to backend/** because Library/ and Website/ keep 52 pre-built bin/
# assemblies under source control. Here we want zero stale bytes in the context,
# so do not narrow these to backend/**.
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/[Dd]ebug/
**/[Rr]elease/
**/x64/
**/x86/
**/artifacts/
**/TestResults/
**/*.trx
**/*.coverage
**/coverage.*.json
**/coverage.*.xml
**/coverage.*.info
**/*.received.*

# Node / Angular output.
# node_modules/ is equally load-bearing: docker/frontend.Dockerfile runs
# `npm ci` before `COPY frontend/ ./`, so a host node_modules would overwrite a
# Linux-native install with host-platform native bindings and defeat the
# deterministic lockfile install.
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/coverage/
**/.angular/
**/npm-debug.log*
**/yarn-error.log*
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/.eslintcache

# Secrets and local environment - never bake credentials into a layer.
# `**/.env*` also covers docker/.env.example: docker-compose interpolates
# docker/.env from the HOST before any build starts, so neither file is ever
# needed inside the context. appsettings.{Development,Production}.json are NOT
# excluded - they are shipped configuration (AAP 0.2.1.1); only *.local.json
# developer overrides are.
**/.env*
**/appsettings.*.local.json
**/*.pfx
**/*.p12
**/*.key
**/*.pem

# IDE / editor / OS noise.
**/.vs/
**/.vscode/
**/.idea/
**/*.user
**/*.userosscache
**/*.userprefs
**/*.suo
**/*.swp
**/*.swo
**/*~
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
**/logs/
**/*.log
